cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use gazeCOM in research, software, or artistic work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "gazeCOM"
abstract: >-
  gazeCOM is an open-source system for saliency-driven iterative image
  generation and composition. Its central method grounds generation in a
  discrete canvas coordinate system: coordinates derived from human input,
  algorithmic movement, computer vision, or a vision-language model determine
  both the image region passed to generation and the placement of each result
  in a persistent composite. The VLM Guide extends this system with
  model-selected placement, prompt decisions, and bounded visual memory.
authors:
  - name: "grebenshyo"
version: "0.3.0"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/grebenshyo/gazecom"
url: "https://grebenshyo.xyz/2026/07/22/gazecom/"
keywords:
